<!--
  sce:std/shared/record_list.scxml — one copy of a shared list of records, a statechart
  of the standard library (docs/adr/0042), written under datamodel="sce-static"
  (docs/SCE_ACCEPTED_SUBSET.md, "Static data model"). Every copy is the same document,
  and no copy is special. A statechart that keeps a list of its own records invokes it as
  a child session (`<invoke type="scxml" src="sce:std/shared/record_list.scxml">`), turns
  each command into the field writes it sends the list, and keeps its own view from what
  the list tells it (below, "What the list tells its parent"); a host may also run it on
  its own.

  A record is a row of fields. The numbers of the rows and of the fields, and what each
  field means, are the application's: the list keeps a number or a text for each and
  reads neither. Each field of each row is a multi-value register: a write gives the
  field one more value, known by the stamp of the write (its dot), and a person who
  writes over a field writes over the values they have SEEN, no others. So two people
  who change the same field of one row at once, neither having seen the other's write,
  both keep theirs, on every copy, whatever order the changes reach it in; and a person
  who writes after seeing them replaces them all. A field with one value reads as that
  value, and with more than one says it was changed twice at once, and which values, for
  a person to choose from.

  The registers are an observed-remove set of the standard `orset_*` algorithms, the
  operation-based form of it (docs/adr/0085): a write is an add of the register's element
  with the write's dot as its tag, and a write-over removes the tag it names. A copy holds
  exactly the adds no write-over has removed, in `adds`, and keeps no tombstone: the layer
  that delivers the changes (below, "Its peers") gives a copy each change once, whole, and
  only after every change its author had taken in when it made it, so a write-over always
  arrives after the write it names, and no write arrives twice. A write-over whose value
  is gone already (another change wrote it over first) changes nothing.
  The element is `id * 65536 + field`: a row is a uint32 and a field a uint16, so the
  pair is one uint64 below 2^48 and no two registers share one, whatever the numbers; it
  is below 2^53 as well, which the Interpreter's integers hold exactly, so no lane meets
  a limit another does not. What a set cannot carry is the value itself, a number and a
  text, so each live add has its value in `values`, beside it, taken in when the add is
  added and taken out when a write-over names it. The standard `mv_value_*` algorithms
  keep them: the record a write's value is read into is what `mv_value_keep` records,
  bounded as its schema says, and `mv_value_drop` forgets. That is the whole of what this
  document adds to the merge.

  The clock is moved by what a copy sees as well as by what it does: a change made after
  reading someone else's sorts after it. A copy's clock is moved once for each change it
  takes in, by the change's stamp: a peer's by a receive, and one of the copy's own node
  (given back to a copy built again, a change of write-overs only among them) up to its
  stamp, so a copy stamps nothing after with a dot it has used (docs/adr/0083, section
  1.6). A state handed over (`record_list.restore`) and the host's word of the highest
  stamp of the copy's own node its delivery layer holds (`record_list.raise`) raise it
  the same way.

  A change is a unit (docs/adr/0046, docs/adr/0085). It is the commands a copy is given
  from the first after the last change ended up to the first that does not say `more`
  (record_edit): each command with `more` is held in `staged` (record_staged), and the one
  that ends the change closes it (`record_list.close`), where the change is judged whole
  (the copy's member may write, no register is written twice, the room, the size),
  stamped once, and turned into its operations (record_op): a write-over of every value
  the copy holds in a register the change names, then a write of every register it
  edits. A change that fails a test is refused whole, with nothing stamped, sent or taken
  in. A change that passes is one message, `record_list.change` (record_change): its
  author, its stamp, which is the dot of every write in it, and its operations in that
  order. A copy that keeps no journal takes it in first, each operation by
  `record_list.take`, an event with no data that reads the next operation of `taking`,
  and sends it after, whole; a copy that keeps one offers it to its host and takes it in
  at the host's verdict (below, "What a copy tells its host"). A change a peer made
  reaches the copy as the same message and is taken in by the same events, so a parent
  is told the change once, and no copy can hold half of one: no half of one is ever on a
  wire.

  A field can be emptied and a row retired (docs/adr/0046, section 2). `record_list.clear`
  (record_clear) writes over every value the copy holds in one register and writes none,
  and `record_list.retire` (record_retire) over every value it holds in any register of a
  row; each is a command of a change as an edit is. Both write over what the copy has
  seen and nothing else, the rule a write over a field has always kept: a value written at
  the same time by someone who had not seen the retire stays, on every copy and in every
  order, and the row then holds the fields such writes gave it, which a parent is told
  (an edit not seen wins). What a retire wrote over goes from `values` and `adds` at once,
  so a retired row takes no room in any copy.

  A copy keeps every list in a room it is built with (`sce:limit`), and a write that
  would pass it fails half way, which no copy can undo. The host therefore gives a list
  less room than the build holds (`record_list.room`), and a copy refuses a change of its
  own whole when the values it would leave pass the room (one that writes no more than it
  writes over never does): before it stamps or sends anything, counted in `full`. The
  room for the changes not yet stable is the delivery layer's, which refuses a change it
  has no room for (record_room). A change that is a person's own is the one judged, and
  what a person sent is taken in as it is, so the room is kept below the build's by what
  the people of one list can write at once.

  Every bound of the list is a name a build may give another number (the limit option
  of sce-codegen, docs/SCE_ACCEPTED_SUBSET.md, "A bound a deployment chooses"), and a
  build that names none is the list as written: `merge_entries` (1024
  adds), `merge_values` (512 values), `merge_text` (the 96 bytes of text a write
  carries and a value keeps), `shared_typed_text` (the 32 bytes of text a person types,
  the type of record_edit's text, which an edit past it is refused at where it is read,
  before the list sees it; a build that raises it keeps `merge_text` at least as large),
  `shared_roster` (64 members), `shared_staged` (32 commands one change stages),
  `shared_parts` (64 operations of one change, the most a `record_list.change` carries)
  and `shared_moved` (64 registers a change moves before they are told, at least
  `shared_parts`, since a change of n operations moves at most n),
  `shared_provisional` (8 changes a copy holds taken in provisionally, docs/adr/0093,
  section 3.4) and `shared_undo` (512 values those changes took out, at least
  `shared_provisional` times `shared_parts`, since each takes out at most as many as it
  has operations). Each name is carried
  by the standard algorithms and schemas the list reads through, so the machine and what
  it calls move together. Every copy of one list is built with the same numbers. A change
  of n operations queues about 2n internal events at once while it is taken in, which a
  C11 build's `SCE_MAX_EVENTS` has to hold (docs/adr/0046, section 6).

  What the list tells its parent. A statechart that invokes the list hands it `announce`
  (`<param name="announce" expr="true"/>`), and from then on the list tells it, once for
  each change it takes in, every register that change moved, whatever its source (a
  person's edit or a peer's change): `record_list.register`
  (record_register) with the row, the field, how many live values the register holds
  (`count`, 0 when every value was written over) and the first of them in the order of
  their dots (register_values), then `record_list.value` (record_value) for each further
  one, with its place in that order (`ordinal`, from 1). An operation that moves a
  register names it to the list itself
  (`record_list.announce`, record_announce), which keeps the registers named in `moved`
  and, for the first of them, raises `record_list.tell`; every operation of the change is
  already waiting before that, so the telling is made once, after the whole change: a
  person's edit, a write-over of each value it saw and then a write, is told as the one
  register it moved, as it stands after the write, and a change of several fields as
  each of them once. A parent may name a register itself by sending the list
  `record_list.announce`, to be told what it holds. A change of its own the list refuses
  is told too, once, after the command that ended it: `record_list.refused`
  (record_refused) with the command at fault (record_command) and why (record_refusal),
  so a parent never takes a change nothing was written for as made (docs/adr/0046,
  docs/adr/0052). A change of a copy that keeps a journal is told by its verdict as
  well (docs/adr/0093, section 3.3): one its delivery layer refused is told as
  `record_list.refused` with the reason the layer gave, `peerRefused` when it gave none;
  one the layer answered `waiting`
  is told as each register it moved and `record_list.pending` (record_pending), and
  later as `record_list.confirmed` (record_confirmed) or, withdrawn, as each register
  the withdrawal moved and `record_list.refused` with `peerRefused` and `withdrawn`.

  A list a host started has no parent, and `#_parent` names no session there: `announce`
  keeps the value its <data> gives it, false, and the list tells no one. The condition is
  what the list keeps of how it was started, and it is read where the telling is made, so
  nothing is sent to `#_parent` by a list no statechart started, whatever asks it to. The
  send names `#_parent` by an expression among the routes it declares (`sce:targets`)
  rather than as a written target: a written `#_parent` makes a machine one that is only
  ever invoked (the C11 backend gives it no entry of its own, and C++ a parent type), and
  this one is started by a host as often as by a parent. `announced` counts the events
  told.

  Its peers. The list sends to its peers by one route and names no peer of its own:
  `#people`, one group every copy sends to and reads (docs/adr/0085, section 3). The
  route is bound to the list's delivery layer, which is not the list: the peer core of a
  host that has one, or the Mesh core's causal route (`delivery: causal`, SCE_MESH.md) for
  a copy that has none. The layer tags each change with its author's number and what its
  author had taken in, gives every copy each change exactly once and only once the copy
  holds every change it follows, repairs what a link lost, and says when a change is
  held everywhere. The list sees none of that: it takes in what it is given, in the order
  it is given it, and its correctness is the layer's order (docs/adr/0085, sections 2
  and 3). What the copy's node is is the host's word (`record_list.join`), and nothing
  of the protocol depends on the number a node is given. The roster is judged on every
  copy: a change whose author the copy's roster does not let write is taken in as no
  change and counted in `denied`.

  What a copy does to itself never waits on what it sends (docs/adr/0046). A send to a
  peer the host gave no route to (no Mesh router: a copy on one device, or one whose link
  was never attached) is `error.execution` where it is made, which ends its block. So in
  every transition the copy queues what it does to itself before it sends anything to a
  peer, and a send to a peer is the last act of its block: a copy with no router takes
  every change it makes in, and counts each send it could not make in `refusals`. A copy
  that keeps a journal sends nothing to a peer, and what it does to itself waits on its
  layer's verdict instead, which is the host's to give (below).

  What a copy tells its host (docs/adr/0083, docs/adr/0093). A copy joined with
  `journal` (the default, record_join) has a delivery layer its host keeps, and takes in
  a change of its own only once that layer has answered for it, so it never holds a
  change its layer refused. It judges and stamps the change as any copy does, holds it
  in `offered`, and offers it to its host on the route `#journal` as
  `record_list.made` (record_made: the change and the host's `command` that ended it).
  The host gives it to the layer, commits the change and its verdict to its journal,
  and gives the copy `record_list.verdict` (record_verdict, record_outcome). Accepted or
  held, the change is taken in; refused, nothing is taken in, the copy holds what it
  held before the close and its clock stays at the stamp, which no change is given
  again; waiting, the change is taken in provisionally, with an undo record of what its
  write-overs took out (`provisional`, record_provisional; `undo`, record_undo), until
  the host confirms it (`record_list.confirm`, record_confirm) or withdraws it
  (`record_list.withdraw`, record_withdraw), which withdraws it and every provisional
  change after it, latest first: the values their writes added go, and the values their
  write-overs took out come back, except one a later write-over took out too. Then the
  copy reports the outcome, `record_list.closed` (record_closed), which it reports at
  once for a change it refused itself or that named nothing. One offer is outstanding
  at a time: a command given while one is is a host's fault, refused where it happens
  and counted in `refusals`, as a verdict, a confirmation or a withdrawal is that names
  no change the copy holds. A copy that holds `shared_provisional` provisional changes
  refuses the next change it closes, `noRoomForHistory`. Peer changes the layer gives
  while an offer is outstanding are taken in as always: they are concurrent with the
  offered change, whose write-overs were fixed when it was closed. `record_list.raise`
  (record_raise) is the host's word of the highest stamp of the copy's own node its
  layer holds, which the clock is raised to. A copy joined with `journal` false, a copy
  a test throws away, reports nothing and takes its change in at once, as a copy with a
  layer that accepts everything would.

  A copy built again is given what was made, never the commands (docs/adr/0083,
  docs/adr/0085, section 4.4): first the stable state its host folded its journal into,
  as `record_list.restore` (record_restore: the live values, each with its own dot, and
  the state's clock), then every change after it, the copy's own and its peers', as
  `record_list.recall` (record_recall), in a causal order; a change of its own the host
  journalled as provisional is recalled so, and taken in provisionally as at its
  verdict. Neither is judged by the roster, reported or sent, and each is told to the
  parent once.

  `values` and `adds` are what a run compares across copies.
-->
<scxml xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml" xmlns:sce="http://sce.dev/ext"
       version="1.0" initial="open" datamodel="sce-static" name="record_list">
  <!-- Every import names its document by its library name, sibling or not: the list is
       read from the library as `sce:std/shared/record_list.scxml`, and also from a file
       a build stands beside other documents, where a relative name would resolve against
       that file's own directory. -->
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="sce:std/shared/record_join.scxml" as="Join"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="sce:std/shared/record_edit.scxml" as="Edit"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="sce:std/shared/record_change.scxml" as="Change"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="sce:std/shared/record_op.scxml" as="Op"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="sce:std/shared/record_staged.scxml" as="Staged"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="sce:std/merge/hlc_timestamp.scxml" as="Hlc"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="sce:std/merge/orset_entry.scxml" as="Entry"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="sce:std/merge/mv_value.scxml" as="Value"/>
  <sce:import kind="algorithm" src="sce:std/merge/hlc_send.scxml" as="HlcSend"/>
  <sce:import kind="algorithm" src="sce:std/merge/hlc_receive.scxml" as="HlcReceive"/>
  <sce:import kind="algorithm" src="sce:std/merge/orset_union.scxml" as="OrsetUnion"/>
  <sce:import kind="algorithm" src="sce:std/merge/orset_live.scxml" as="OrsetLive"/>
  <sce:import kind="algorithm" src="sce:std/merge/mv_value_holds.scxml" as="MvValueHolds"/>
  <sce:import kind="algorithm" src="sce:std/merge/mv_value_keep.scxml" as="MvValueKeep"/>
  <sce:import kind="algorithm" src="sce:std/merge/mv_value_drop.scxml" as="MvValueDrop"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="sce:std/shared/record_room.scxml" as="Room"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="sce:std/shared/record_role.scxml" as="Role"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="sce:std/shared/record_member.scxml" as="Member"/>
  <sce:import kind="algorithm" src="sce:std/shared/record_roster.scxml" as="RecordRoster"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="sce:std/shared/record_announce.scxml" as="Announce"/>
  <sce:import kind="algorithm" src="sce:std/shared/register_values.scxml" as="RegisterValues"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="sce:std/shared/record_clear.scxml" as="Clear"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="sce:std/shared/record_retire.scxml" as="Retire"/>
  <sce:import kind="enum" src="sce:std/shared/record_command.scxml" as="Command"/>
  <sce:import kind="enum" src="sce:std/shared/record_refusal.scxml" as="Refusal"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="sce:std/shared/record_refused.scxml" as="Refused"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="sce:std/shared/record_made.scxml" as="Made"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="sce:std/shared/record_closed.scxml" as="Closed"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="sce:std/shared/record_verdict.scxml" as="Verdict"/>
  <sce:import kind="enum" src="sce:std/shared/record_outcome.scxml" as="Outcome"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="sce:std/shared/record_confirm.scxml" as="Confirm"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="sce:std/shared/record_withdraw.scxml" as="Withdraw"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="sce:std/shared/record_raise.scxml" as="ClockRaise"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="sce:std/shared/record_pending.scxml" as="Pending"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="sce:std/shared/record_confirmed.scxml" as="Confirmed"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="sce:std/shared/record_recall.scxml" as="Recall"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="sce:std/shared/record_restore.scxml" as="Restore"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="sce:std/shared/record_provisional.scxml" as="Provisional"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="sce:std/shared/record_undo.scxml" as="Undo"/>
  <datamodel>
    <data id="node" sce:type="uint64" expr="0" sce:direction="out"/>
    <!-- Whether the host keeps a journal of what each change made (record_join): a copy
         keeps one unless it is joined without. -->
    <data id="journal" sce:type="bool" expr="true"/>
    <data id="clock" sce:type="record:Hlc" sce:direction="out">
      <sce:set name="wallTime" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="counter" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="nodeId" expr="0"/>
    </data>
    <data id="stamp" sce:type="record:Hlc">
      <sce:set name="wallTime" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="counter" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="nodeId" expr="0"/>
    </data>
    <!-- The change in hand: its stamp, which is the dot of every write in it, with its
         author as the dot's node. Every operation of one change is taken in before
         anything else reaches the copy, so the operations in `taking` are read with it. -->
    <data id="dot" sce:type="record:Hlc">
      <sce:set name="wallTime" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="counter" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="nodeId" expr="0"/>
    </data>
    <!-- The bounds of the lists a deployment may move are named (`sce:limit`): the
         lists of entries and of values are as large as the standard algorithms that
         return them, which carry the same names, so a build that gives a name a number
         moves the machine and the algorithms together. -->
    <data id="adds" sce:type="list&lt;record:Entry&gt;[merge_entries=1024]" sce:direction="out"/>
    <data id="one" sce:type="list&lt;record:Entry&gt;[merge_entries=1024]"/>
    <data id="entry" sce:type="record:Entry">
      <sce:set name="element" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="wallTime" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="counter" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="nodeId" expr="0"/>
    </data>
    <data id="values" sce:type="list&lt;record:Value&gt;[merge_values=512]" sce:direction="out"/>
    <data id="held" sce:type="record:Value">
      <sce:set name="id" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="field" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="value" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="text" expr="''"/>
      <sce:set name="wallTime" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="counter" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="nodeId" expr="0"/>
    </data>
    <data id="shareId" sce:type="uint32" expr="0"/>
    <data id="shareField" sce:type="uint16" expr="0"/>
    <data id="wasLive" sce:type="bool" expr="false"/>
    <data id="present" sce:type="bool" expr="false"/>
    <data id="refusals" sce:type="uint32" expr="0" sce:direction="out"/>
    <!-- How many values the host lets this copy hold (record_list.room), 0 for no limit,
         and the changes a person made that were refused for it (`full`). -->
    <data id="roomValues" sce:type="uint32" expr="0"/>
    <data id="full" sce:type="uint32" expr="0" sce:direction="out"/>
    <!-- What the host lets each member do (record_list.role), the changes that were
         refused for it (`denied`, a person's own and a peer's alike) and what the change
         in hand is judged by: whether its author may write. -->
    <data id="roster" sce:type="list&lt;record:Member&gt;[shared_roster=64]"/>
    <data id="denied" sce:type="uint32" expr="0" sce:direction="out"/>
    <data id="forbidden" sce:type="bool" expr="false"/>
    <data id="authorized" sce:type="bool" expr="true"/>
    <!-- What the list tells the statechart that invoked it: `announce`, handed by the
         <invoke> that starts the list and false for a list a host started, which tells
         no one; `announced`, the events told; and what the telling in hand reads, the
         live values of one register in the order of their dots and the place of each. -->
    <data id="announce" sce:type="bool" expr="false"/>
    <data id="announced" sce:type="uint32" expr="0" sce:direction="out"/>
    <!-- The registers the change in hand moved, by their element, kept until the change
         is told, and whether the one named now is among them already. -->
    <data id="moved" sce:type="list&lt;uint64&gt;[shared_moved=64]"/>
    <data id="listed" sce:type="bool" expr="false"/>
    <data id="live" sce:type="list&lt;record:Value&gt;[merge_values=512]"/>
    <data id="ordinal" sce:type="uint32" expr="0"/>
    <!-- What a register that holds no value is told as: the number 0, no text and the
         dot of no write, each of its field's own type. -->
    <data id="empty" sce:type="record:Value">
      <sce:set name="id" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="field" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="value" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="text" expr="''"/>
      <sce:set name="wallTime" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="counter" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="nodeId" expr="0"/>
    </data>
    <!-- A change (docs/adr/0046): the commands of the change in hand (`staged`), whether
         the command in hand says the change goes on (`holding`), the `now` of the one that
         ends it, whether the change is refused (`spoiled`), and whether the statement in
         hand is one whose failure refuses it (`probing`): a list past its room fails as
         an assignment does, ending the block, and
         error.execution is where the change is then refused. What a change is judged by:
         the values it writes over (`gone`), the registers it writes (`writes`), and
         whether the value in hand is in a register it names (`covered`). -->
    <data id="staged" sce:type="list&lt;record:Staged&gt;[shared_staged=32]"/>
    <data id="staging" sce:type="record:Staged">
      <sce:set name="kind" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="id" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="field" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="value" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="text" expr="''"/>
    </data>
    <data id="holding" sce:type="bool" expr="false"/>
    <data id="closingNow" sce:type="int64" expr="0"/>
    <data id="spoiled" sce:type="bool" expr="false"/>
    <data id="probing" sce:type="bool" expr="false"/>
    <data id="gone" sce:type="uint32" expr="0"/>
    <data id="writes" sce:type="uint32" expr="0"/>
    <data id="covered" sce:type="bool" expr="false"/>
    <!-- What a refused change is told to the parent as (record_list.refused): why the
         statement in hand would refuse it if it failed (`probe`), why it was refused
         (`spoiledFor`), and the command at fault (`namedId`, `namedField`, and
         `namedKind`, the command it was). -->
    <data id="probe" sce:type="enum:Refusal" expr="Refusal.changeTooLarge"/>
    <data id="spoiledFor" sce:type="enum:Refusal" expr="Refusal.changeTooLarge"/>
    <data id="namedId" sce:type="uint32" expr="0"/>
    <data id="namedField" sce:type="uint16" expr="0"/>
    <data id="namedKind" sce:type="enum:Command" expr="Command.edit"/>
    <!-- The operations of the change in hand (`taking`), in the order of the change, the
         next to take in at `took`, each read by an event of its own that carries no data;
         and the operation in hand (`op`). A change of the copy's own is sent from
         `taking` whole once every operation of it is taken in. -->
    <data id="taking" sce:type="list&lt;record:Op&gt;[shared_parts=64]"/>
    <data id="took" sce:type="uint32" expr="0"/>
    <data id="op" sce:type="record:Op">
      <sce:set name="kind" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="id" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="field" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="value" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="text" expr="''"/>
      <sce:set name="wallTime" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="counter" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="nodeId" expr="0"/>
    </data>
    <!-- How the operations in `taking` are taken in: as a state handed over, each write
         at the dot it carries (`restoring`, record_list.restore), and as a change of the
         copy's own taken in provisionally, whose write-overs keep what they take out in
         the undo record (`tentative`). -->
    <data id="restoring" sce:type="bool" expr="false"/>
    <data id="tentative" sce:type="bool" expr="false"/>
    <!-- A change of a copy that keeps a journal (docs/adr/0093): the host's name for the
         command in hand, kept before anything can fail, so the one that ends a change
         names it (`closingCommand`); the change offered to the host and not answered
         yet, its operations (`offered`, empty when none is) and its stamp
         (`offeredAt`); why its layer refused it, as its verdict says (`refusedFor`);
         and what is reported of the change that ended (record_closed):
         how many operations were taken in (`closedOps`), why it was refused (`closedFor`,
         absent for a change taken in or one that named nothing) and its stamp
         (`closedAt`, 0 when nothing was stamped). -->
    <data id="closingCommand" sce:type="uint64" expr="0"/>
    <data id="offered" sce:type="list&lt;record:Op&gt;[shared_parts=64]"/>
    <data id="offeredAt" sce:type="record:Hlc">
      <sce:set name="wallTime" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="counter" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="nodeId" expr="0"/>
    </data>
    <data id="refusedFor" sce:type="enum:Refusal" expr="Refusal.peerRefused"/>
    <data id="closedOps" sce:type="uint32" expr="0"/>
    <data id="closedFor" sce:type="optional&lt;enum:Refusal&gt;" expr="null"/>
    <data id="closedAt" sce:type="record:Hlc">
      <sce:set name="wallTime" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="counter" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="nodeId" expr="0"/>
    </data>
    <!-- The changes of the copy's own taken in provisionally, in the order they were
         taken in (`provisional`), and the values their write-overs took out (`undo`),
         until the host confirms or withdraws each (docs/adr/0093, section 3.4); the
         change named now (`standing`), whether the host's word named one the copy holds
         (`provisionalFound`) and where the changes to withdraw begin (`withdrawFrom`); and what is
         kept of each list while one is rebuilt without what leaves it. -->
    <data id="provisional" sce:type="list&lt;record:Provisional&gt;[shared_provisional=8]"/>
    <data id="provisionalKept" sce:type="list&lt;record:Provisional&gt;[shared_provisional=8]"/>
    <data id="standing" sce:type="record:Provisional">
      <sce:set name="wallTime" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="counter" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="command" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="id" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="field" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="kind" expr="Command.edit"/>
    </data>
    <data id="provisionalFound" sce:type="bool" expr="false"/>
    <data id="withdrawFrom" sce:type="uint32" expr="0"/>
    <data id="undo" sce:type="list&lt;record:Undo&gt;[shared_undo=512]"/>
    <data id="undoKept" sce:type="list&lt;record:Undo&gt;[shared_undo=512]"/>
    <data id="undoing" sce:type="record:Undo">
      <sce:set name="atWallTime" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="atCounter" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="id" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="field" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="value" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="text" expr="''"/>
      <sce:set name="wallTime" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="counter" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="nodeId" expr="0"/>
    </data>
  </datamodel>
  <state id="open">
    <transition event="record_list.join" type="internal">
      <assign location="node" expr="_event.data.node"/>
      <assign location="journal" expr="_event.data.journal"/>
    </transition>

    <!-- How many values the host lets this copy hold (record_list.room). 0 is no limit.
         The room for the changes not yet stable is the delivery layer's, and the list
         reads no count of them (record_room). -->
    <transition event="record_list.room" type="internal">
      <assign location="roomValues" expr="_event.data.values"/>
    </transition>

    <!-- What the host lets a member do (record_list.role): the member takes the role, or
         is taken off the roster by a role of 0. A copy with no roster refuses no one, and
         one with a roster refuses a change of its own member's that is not a writer's,
         and takes a peer's change whose author is not a writer as no change. The roster
         is the host's word and the copies take it alike, as they take the room. -->
    <transition event="record_list.role" type="internal">
      <assign location="roster" expr="RecordRoster(roster, _event.data.node, _event.data.role)"/>
    </transition>

    <!-- A command given while a change the copy offered its host is not answered yet is
         the host's fault (docs/adr/0093, section 3.2): a change made now would be
         prepared on a state that lacks the one before it. It is refused where it
         happens, stages nothing, and is counted in `refusals`. These come before the
         commands' own transitions, which they are taken in place of. -->
    <transition event="record_list.edit" cond="len(offered) &gt; 0" type="internal">
      <assign location="refusals" expr="refusals + 1"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="record_list.clear" cond="len(offered) &gt; 0" type="internal">
      <assign location="refusals" expr="refusals + 1"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="record_list.retire" cond="len(offered) &gt; 0" type="internal">
      <assign location="refusals" expr="refusals + 1"/>
    </transition>

    <!-- A person's edit of one field: a command of a change (docs/adr/0046). It is
         staged, and the command that does not say `more` ends the change, which
         `record_list.close` judges, stamps and takes in whole. A change past the room of
         `staged` fails the append, which ends the block, and error.execution refuses the
         change. A text past what a person writes never reaches here: record_edit's text
         is of that bound, and an edit past it is refused whole where it is read
         (docs/adr/0086, section 4.4). Nothing is stamped or sent here. A change already
         refused stages nothing more, and is ended all the same. The host's name for the
         command is kept before anything can fail, so the one that ends the change is
         named in what is reported of it, refused or not. -->
    <transition event="record_list.edit" type="internal">
      <assign location="closingCommand" expr="_event.data.command"/>
      <assign location="holding" expr="_event.data.more"/>
      <if cond="!spoiled">
        <assign location="namedId" expr="_event.data.id"/>
        <assign location="namedField" expr="_event.data.field"/>
        <assign location="namedKind" expr="Command.edit"/>
        <assign location="probing" expr="true"/>
        <assign location="staging.kind" expr="0"/>
        <assign location="staging.id" expr="_event.data.id"/>
        <assign location="staging.field" expr="_event.data.field"/>
        <assign location="staging.value" expr="_event.data.value"/>
        <assign location="staging.text" expr="_event.data.text"/>
        <assign location="probe" expr="Refusal.changeTooLarge"/>
        <sce:append target="staged" expr="staging"/>
        <assign location="probing" expr="false"/>
      </if>
      <if cond="!holding">
        <assign location="closingNow" expr="_event.data.now"/>
        <send target="#_internal" event="record_list.close"/>
      </if>
    </transition>

    <!-- A person's word that a field is to hold nothing: a command of a change, staged as
         an edit is, which writes over every value the copy holds in the field when the
         change is taken in, and writes none. -->
    <transition event="record_list.clear" type="internal">
      <assign location="closingCommand" expr="_event.data.command"/>
      <assign location="holding" expr="_event.data.more"/>
      <if cond="!spoiled">
        <assign location="namedId" expr="_event.data.id"/>
        <assign location="namedField" expr="_event.data.field"/>
        <assign location="namedKind" expr="Command.clear"/>
        <assign location="probing" expr="true"/>
        <assign location="probe" expr="Refusal.changeTooLarge"/>
        <assign location="staging.kind" expr="1"/>
        <assign location="staging.id" expr="_event.data.id"/>
        <assign location="staging.field" expr="_event.data.field"/>
        <assign location="staging.value" expr="0"/>
        <assign location="staging.text" expr="''"/>
        <sce:append target="staged" expr="staging"/>
        <assign location="probing" expr="false"/>
      </if>
      <if cond="!holding">
        <assign location="closingNow" expr="_event.data.now"/>
        <send target="#_internal" event="record_list.close"/>
      </if>
    </transition>

    <!-- A person's word that a row is gone: a command of a change, staged as an edit is,
         which writes over every value the copy holds in any field of the row when the
         change is taken in, and writes none. -->
    <transition event="record_list.retire" type="internal">
      <assign location="closingCommand" expr="_event.data.command"/>
      <assign location="holding" expr="_event.data.more"/>
      <if cond="!spoiled">
        <assign location="namedId" expr="_event.data.id"/>
        <assign location="namedField" expr="0"/>
        <assign location="namedKind" expr="Command.retire"/>
        <assign location="probing" expr="true"/>
        <assign location="probe" expr="Refusal.changeTooLarge"/>
        <assign location="staging.kind" expr="2"/>
        <assign location="staging.id" expr="_event.data.id"/>
        <assign location="staging.field" expr="0"/>
        <assign location="staging.value" expr="0"/>
        <assign location="staging.text" expr="''"/>
        <sce:append target="staged" expr="staging"/>
        <assign location="probing" expr="false"/>
      </if>
      <if cond="!holding">
        <assign location="closingNow" expr="_event.data.now"/>
        <send target="#_internal" event="record_list.close"/>
      </if>
    </transition>

    <!-- The change in hand is ended: judged whole, and taken in, or refused whole.

         It is refused when the copy's member may not write (record_list.role: with no
         roster set, anyone may; with one, a member whose role is a writer's), counted in
         `denied`; when two of its commands write or clear one register, since the order
         of a change's commands means nothing; and when the values it would leave pass
         the room the host gave the copy (record_list.room), counted in `full` (a change
         that writes no more values than it writes over adds none). A change that names
         nothing the copy holds and writes nothing is no change, and is never sent.

         A change that passes is stamped once, with the `now` of the command that ended
         it, and turned into its operations in `taking`: a write-over of each value the
         copy holds in a register the change names, in the order of `adds`, each naming
         the dot of the value it writes over, then a write of each register it edits, in
         the order of its commands. A write carries no dot of its own: its dot is the
         change's stamp, which the change carries once, so its `wallTime`, `counter` and
         `nodeId` are 0 (record_op). A change of more operations than `taking` holds is
         refused whole, by error.execution, before the clock moves. Then, by a copy that
         keeps no journal, every operation is queued to be taken in here, and after them
         the change is queued to be sent: the copy holds the change before it sends it.
         A copy that keeps one holds the change offered instead, and queues its offer to
         the host (docs/adr/0093, section 3.1): it takes the change in at the verdict. Such
         a copy refuses a change it closes while it holds as many provisional changes as
         it has room for (`shared_provisional`), `noRoomForHistory`: its layer may hold
         the change not yet carried, and the copy could not take it in provisionally. The
         outcome of a change refused here, or of one that named nothing, is reported to
         the host at once. -->
    <transition event="record_list.close" type="internal">
      <if cond="!spoiled &amp;&amp; len(roster) &gt; 0">
        <assign location="forbidden" expr="true"/>
        <foreach array="roster" item="m">
          <if cond="m.node === node &amp;&amp; m.role &gt;= 2">
            <assign location="forbidden" expr="false"/>
          </if>
        </foreach>
        <if cond="forbidden">
          <assign location="denied" expr="denied + 1"/>
          <assign location="spoiled" expr="true"/>
          <assign location="spoiledFor" expr="Refusal.notWriter"/>
        </if>
      </if>
      <if cond="!spoiled">
        <foreach array="staged" item="earlier" index="earlierAt">
          <foreach array="staged" item="later" index="laterAt">
            <if cond="!spoiled &amp;&amp; laterAt &gt; earlierAt &amp;&amp; earlier.kind !== 2 &amp;&amp; later.kind !== 2 &amp;&amp; earlier.id === later.id &amp;&amp; earlier.field === later.field">
              <assign location="spoiled" expr="true"/>
              <assign location="spoiledFor" expr="Refusal.registerNamedTwice"/>
              <assign location="namedId" expr="later.id"/>
              <assign location="namedField" expr="later.field"/>
              <!-- Neither is a retire, so the second is an edit or a clear. -->
              <if cond="later.kind === 1">
                <assign location="namedKind" expr="Command.clear"/>
              <else/>
                <assign location="namedKind" expr="Command.edit"/>
              </if>
            </if>
          </foreach>
        </foreach>
      </if>
      <assign location="gone" expr="0"/>
      <assign location="writes" expr="0"/>
      <if cond="!spoiled">
        <foreach array="adds" item="a">
          <assign location="covered" expr="false"/>
          <foreach array="staged" item="s">
            <if cond="a.element / 65536 === s.id &amp;&amp; (s.kind === 2 || a.element % 65536 === s.field)">
              <assign location="covered" expr="true"/>
            </if>
          </foreach>
          <if cond="covered">
            <assign location="gone" expr="gone + 1"/>
          </if>
        </foreach>
        <foreach array="staged" item="s">
          <if cond="s.kind === 0">
            <assign location="writes" expr="writes + 1"/>
          </if>
        </foreach>
      </if>
      <if cond="!spoiled &amp;&amp; gone + writes &gt; 0 &amp;&amp; roomValues &gt; 0 &amp;&amp; writes &gt; gone &amp;&amp; len(values) + writes &gt; roomValues + gone">
        <assign location="full" expr="full + 1"/>
        <assign location="spoiled" expr="true"/>
        <assign location="spoiledFor" expr="Refusal.noRoomForValue"/>
      </if>
      <if cond="!spoiled &amp;&amp; journal &amp;&amp; gone + writes &gt; 0 &amp;&amp; len(provisional) &gt;= _x.limits.shared_provisional">
        <assign location="spoiled" expr="true"/>
        <assign location="spoiledFor" expr="Refusal.noRoomForHistory"/>
      </if>
      <if cond="!spoiled &amp;&amp; gone + writes &gt; 0">
        <assign location="probing" expr="true"/>
        <assign location="probe" expr="Refusal.clockExhausted"/>
        <assign location="stamp" expr="HlcSend(clock, closingNow, node)"/>
        <assign location="probe" expr="Refusal.changeTooLarge"/>
        <sce:clear target="taking"/>
        <assign location="took" expr="0"/>
        <foreach array="adds" item="a">
          <assign location="covered" expr="false"/>
          <foreach array="staged" item="s">
            <if cond="a.element / 65536 === s.id &amp;&amp; (s.kind === 2 || a.element % 65536 === s.field)">
              <assign location="covered" expr="true"/>
            </if>
          </foreach>
          <if cond="covered">
            <assign location="op.kind" expr="1"/>
            <assign location="op.id" expr="a.element / 65536"/>
            <assign location="op.field" expr="a.element % 65536"/>
            <assign location="op.value" expr="0"/>
            <assign location="op.text" expr="''"/>
            <assign location="op.wallTime" expr="a.wallTime"/>
            <assign location="op.counter" expr="a.counter"/>
            <assign location="op.nodeId" expr="a.nodeId"/>
            <sce:append target="taking" expr="op"/>
          </if>
        </foreach>
        <foreach array="staged" item="s">
          <if cond="s.kind === 0">
            <assign location="op.kind" expr="0"/>
            <assign location="op.id" expr="s.id"/>
            <assign location="op.field" expr="s.field"/>
            <assign location="op.value" expr="s.value"/>
            <assign location="op.text" expr="s.text"/>
            <assign location="op.wallTime" expr="0"/>
            <assign location="op.counter" expr="0"/>
            <assign location="op.nodeId" expr="0"/>
            <sce:append target="taking" expr="op"/>
          </if>
        </foreach>
        <assign location="probing" expr="false"/>
        <sce:clear target="staged"/>
        <assign location="clock" expr="stamp"/>
        <assign location="dot" expr="stamp"/>
        <if cond="!journal">
          <assign location="restoring" expr="false"/>
          <assign location="tentative" expr="false"/>
          <foreach array="taking" item="t">
            <send target="#_internal" event="record_list.take"/>
          </foreach>
          <send target="#_internal" event="record_list.pass"/>
        </if>
        <if cond="journal">
          <sce:clear target="offered"/>
          <foreach array="taking" item="t">
            <sce:append target="offered" expr="t"/>
          </foreach>
          <assign location="offeredAt" expr="stamp"/>
          <send target="#_internal" event="record_list.offer"/>
        </if>
      </if>
      <!-- A change that named nothing the copy holds is no change; a copy that keeps a
           journal says so, as an outcome with no operation and no refusal. -->
      <if cond="!spoiled &amp;&amp; gone + writes === 0">
        <sce:clear target="staged"/>
        <if cond="journal">
          <assign location="closedOps" expr="0"/>
          <assign location="closedFor" expr="null"/>
          <assign location="closedAt.wallTime" expr="0"/>
          <assign location="closedAt.counter" expr="0"/>
          <assign location="closedAt.nodeId" expr="0"/>
          <send target="#_internal" event="record_list.conclude"/>
        </if>
      </if>
      <!-- A refused change is dropped whole and told to the statechart that invoked the
           list, once, with the command at fault and why (record_refused); a list a host
           started tells no one. A copy that keeps a journal reports it to its host as
           well, as the outcome of the command that ended it, queued before the parent is
           sent anything. -->
      <if cond="spoiled">
        <sce:clear target="staged"/>
        <assign location="spoiled" expr="false"/>
        <if cond="journal">
          <assign location="closedOps" expr="0"/>
          <assign location="closedFor" expr="spoiledFor"/>
          <assign location="closedAt.wallTime" expr="0"/>
          <assign location="closedAt.counter" expr="0"/>
          <assign location="closedAt.nodeId" expr="0"/>
          <send target="#_internal" event="record_list.conclude"/>
        </if>
        <if cond="announce">
          <send event="record_list.refused" targetexpr="'#_parent'" sce:targets="#_parent">
            <param name="id" expr="namedId"/>
            <param name="field" expr="namedField"/>
            <param name="kind" expr="namedKind"/>
            <param name="reason" expr="spoiledFor"/>
            <param name="command" expr="closingCommand"/>
            <param name="withdrawn" expr="false"/>
          </send>
        </if>
      </if>
    </transition>

    <!-- The change a copy that keeps a journal closed, offered to its host on the route
         `#journal` (record_made, docs/adr/0093, section 3.1): its author, its stamp, its
         operations and the host's name for the command that ended it. The host gives it
         to the change's delivery layer and the copy its verdict. The send is the whole of
         the block, so one that fails where it is made fails alone. -->
    <transition event="record_list.offer" type="internal">
      <send target="#journal" event="record_list.made">
        <param name="by" expr="offeredAt.nodeId"/>
        <param name="wallTime" expr="offeredAt.wallTime"/>
        <param name="counter" expr="offeredAt.counter"/>
        <param name="ops" expr="offered"/>
        <param name="command" expr="closingCommand"/>
      </send>
    </transition>

    <!-- The verdict of the copy's delivery layer on the change it offered (record_verdict,
         docs/adr/0093, section 3.3), given by the host once it has journalled it, naming
         the change by its stamp. Every outcome but a refusal takes the change in, each
         operation by `record_list.take` in the change's order, before the outcome is
         reported (record_closed): accepted and held alike, and waiting provisionally,
         its stamp, the host's command and what its refusal would be told as kept in
         `provisional`, and its write-overs keeping what they take out in `undo`; a
         parent is told the registers once the change is whole, and that the change is
         pending. A refusal takes nothing in: the copy holds what it held before the
         close, its clock stays at the stamp, which no change is given again, and the
         parent is told why, the layer's reason or `peerRefused` when it gives none
         (`noRoomForHistory` for a layer whose log is full, docs/adr/0085, section 3).
         The clock is not moved: it was moved to the stamp when the change was closed. A
         change the layer refused, or one withdrawn, is told as the register of its first
         operation, a write as an edit and a write-over as a clear, since no command of it
         is at fault, and the change itself is named the same way after a restart
         (record_refused). -->
    <transition event="record_list.verdict" cond="len(offered) &gt; 0 &amp;&amp; _event.data.outcome !== Outcome.none &amp;&amp; _event.data.wallTime === offeredAt.wallTime &amp;&amp; _event.data.counter === offeredAt.counter" type="internal">
      <assign location="standing.wallTime" expr="offeredAt.wallTime"/>
      <assign location="standing.counter" expr="offeredAt.counter"/>
      <assign location="standing.command" expr="closingCommand"/>
      <assign location="standing.id" expr="offered[0].id"/>
      <assign location="standing.field" expr="offered[0].field"/>
      <if cond="offered[0].kind === 0">
        <assign location="standing.kind" expr="Command.edit"/>
      <else/>
        <assign location="standing.kind" expr="Command.clear"/>
      </if>
      <assign location="closedAt" expr="offeredAt"/>
      <if cond="_event.data.outcome === Outcome.refused">
        <assign location="refusedFor" expr="_event.data.reason ?? Refusal.peerRefused"/>
        <assign location="closedOps" expr="0"/>
        <assign location="closedFor" expr="refusedFor"/>
        <sce:clear target="offered"/>
        <send target="#_internal" event="record_list.conclude"/>
        <if cond="announce">
          <send event="record_list.refused" targetexpr="'#_parent'" sce:targets="#_parent">
            <param name="id" expr="standing.id"/>
            <param name="field" expr="standing.field"/>
            <param name="kind" expr="standing.kind"/>
            <param name="reason" expr="refusedFor"/>
            <param name="command" expr="standing.command"/>
            <param name="withdrawn" expr="false"/>
          </send>
        </if>
      </if>
      <if cond="_event.data.outcome !== Outcome.refused">
        <assign location="closedOps" expr="len(offered)"/>
        <assign location="closedFor" expr="null"/>
        <sce:clear target="taking"/>
        <foreach array="offered" item="t">
          <sce:append target="taking" expr="t"/>
        </foreach>
        <assign location="took" expr="0"/>
        <assign location="dot" expr="offeredAt"/>
        <assign location="restoring" expr="false"/>
        <assign location="tentative" expr="_event.data.outcome === Outcome.waiting"/>
        <if cond="tentative">
          <sce:append target="provisional" expr="standing"/>
        </if>
        <sce:clear target="offered"/>
        <foreach array="taking" item="t">
          <send target="#_internal" event="record_list.take"/>
        </foreach>
        <send target="#_internal" event="record_list.conclude"/>
        <if cond="tentative &amp;&amp; announce">
          <send event="record_list.pending" targetexpr="'#_parent'" sce:targets="#_parent">
            <param name="wallTime" expr="standing.wallTime"/>
            <param name="counter" expr="standing.counter"/>
            <param name="command" expr="standing.command"/>
          </send>
        </if>
      </if>
    </transition>

    <!-- A verdict that names no change the copy holds offered, or that is no verdict
         (`none`), is the host's fault: it changes nothing and is counted. -->
    <transition event="record_list.verdict" type="internal">
      <assign location="refusals" expr="refusals + 1"/>
    </transition>

    <!-- The outcome of the change that ended, reported to the host's journal
         (record_closed): taken in, refused or naming nothing, so the host's record of
         the command that ended it always has one. -->
    <transition event="record_list.conclude" type="internal">
      <send target="#journal" event="record_list.closed">
        <param name="command" expr="closingCommand"/>
        <param name="operations" expr="closedOps"/>
        <param name="reason" expr="closedFor"/>
        <param name="wallTime" expr="closedAt.wallTime"/>
        <param name="counter" expr="closedAt.counter"/>
      </send>
    </transition>

    <!-- A peer's change, as the delivery layer gives it: once, whole, and after every
         change its author had taken in when it made it (docs/adr/0085, section 3). Its
         author is judged against the roster, on every copy: one the roster does not let
         write is taken in as no change, counted in `denied`. Otherwise the change becomes
         the change in hand and is delivered (record_list.deliver). -->
    <transition event="record_list.change" type="internal">
      <assign location="authorized" expr="true"/>
      <if cond="len(roster) &gt; 0">
        <assign location="authorized" expr="false"/>
        <foreach array="roster" item="m">
          <if cond="m.node === _event.data.by &amp;&amp; m.role &gt;= 2">
            <assign location="authorized" expr="true"/>
          </if>
        </foreach>
      </if>
      <if cond="!authorized">
        <assign location="denied" expr="denied + 1"/>
      </if>
      <if cond="authorized">
        <assign location="taking" expr="_event.data.ops"/>
        <assign location="took" expr="0"/>
        <assign location="dot.wallTime" expr="_event.data.wallTime"/>
        <assign location="dot.counter" expr="_event.data.counter"/>
        <assign location="dot.nodeId" expr="_event.data.by"/>
        <assign location="restoring" expr="false"/>
        <assign location="tentative" expr="false"/>
        <send target="#_internal" event="record_list.deliver"/>
      </if>
    </transition>

    <!-- A change the host recorded, given back to a copy it builds again (record_recall,
         docs/adr/0083, section 1.5; docs/adr/0085, section 7.2): the copy's own, as it
         offered it, or another's, as the host's delivery layer holds it, in a causal
         order. It becomes the change in hand and is delivered as a peer's change is, by
         the one path every change is taken in by, and is not judged by the roster: it
         was admitted where it was made or carried. Nothing is reported or sent, so a copy
         built again sends nothing while it is. A change of the copy's own the host
         journalled as provisional is taken in provisionally, as at its verdict, and is
         kept in `provisional` with what its withdrawal would be told as (docs/adr/0093,
         section 3.5); the flag is not read of another's change. -->
    <transition event="record_list.recall" type="internal">
      <assign location="taking" expr="_event.data.ops"/>
      <assign location="took" expr="0"/>
      <assign location="dot.wallTime" expr="_event.data.wallTime"/>
      <assign location="dot.counter" expr="_event.data.counter"/>
      <assign location="dot.nodeId" expr="_event.data.by"/>
      <assign location="restoring" expr="false"/>
      <assign location="tentative" expr="_event.data.provisional &amp;&amp; _event.data.by === node"/>
      <if cond="tentative">
        <assign location="standing.wallTime" expr="_event.data.wallTime"/>
        <assign location="standing.counter" expr="_event.data.counter"/>
        <assign location="standing.command" expr="_event.data.command"/>
        <assign location="standing.id" expr="taking[0].id"/>
        <assign location="standing.field" expr="taking[0].field"/>
        <if cond="taking[0].kind === 0">
          <assign location="standing.kind" expr="Command.edit"/>
        <else/>
          <assign location="standing.kind" expr="Command.clear"/>
        </if>
        <sce:append target="provisional" expr="standing"/>
      </if>
      <send target="#_internal" event="record_list.deliver"/>
    </transition>

    <!-- The change in hand (`taking`, `dot`), a peer's or a recalled one, delivered:
         every operation is queued to be taken in, in the order of the change, and then
         the clock is moved by the change's stamp, once: a peer's change by `hlc_receive`;
         a change of this copy's own node, which a copy built again or started again from
         an older save is given back, up to its stamp, a change of write-overs only among
         them (docs/adr/0083, section 1.6), so that what the copy stamps next is after it
         and never with a dot it has used. The clock is moved last, so a clock that
         cannot move ends a block that has queued the change already. -->
    <transition event="record_list.deliver" type="internal">
      <foreach array="taking" item="t">
        <send target="#_internal" event="record_list.take"/>
      </foreach>
      <if cond="dot.nodeId === node &amp;&amp; (dot.wallTime &gt; clock.wallTime || (dot.wallTime === clock.wallTime &amp;&amp; dot.counter &gt; clock.counter))">
        <assign location="clock.wallTime" expr="dot.wallTime"/>
        <assign location="clock.counter" expr="dot.counter"/>
      </if>
      <if cond="dot.nodeId !== node">
        <assign location="clock" expr="HlcReceive(clock, dot, clock.wallTime, node)"/>
      </if>
    </transition>

    <!-- A stable state, handed to a copy its host builds again before the changes after
         it (record_restore, docs/adr/0085, section 4.4): its live values, each a write at
         the dot it carries, taken in by the one path every operation is, and the state's
         clock, which the copy's clock is raised to as to a stamp of its own, and never by
         a receive. It claims no change's identity: it is judged by no roster, reported
         and sent to no one, and told to the parent once. A value held already moves
         nothing, so a state given in several parts is taken in whole in any order. -->
    <transition event="record_list.restore" type="internal">
      <assign location="taking" expr="_event.data.ops"/>
      <assign location="took" expr="0"/>
      <assign location="restoring" expr="true"/>
      <assign location="tentative" expr="false"/>
      <foreach array="taking" item="t">
        <send target="#_internal" event="record_list.take"/>
      </foreach>
      <if cond="_event.data.wallTime &gt; clock.wallTime || (_event.data.wallTime === clock.wallTime &amp;&amp; _event.data.counter &gt; clock.counter)">
        <assign location="clock.wallTime" expr="_event.data.wallTime"/>
        <assign location="clock.counter" expr="_event.data.counter"/>
      </if>
    </transition>

    <!-- The highest stamp of the copy's own node its delivery layer holds, as the host
         gives it (record_raise, docs/adr/0093, section 4.3): the clock is raised to it as
         to a stamp of the copy's own, never by a receive, since it is no peer's. A stamp
         at or below the clock moves nothing; the next change is stamped after it. -->
    <transition event="record_list.raise" type="internal">
      <if cond="_event.data.wallTime &gt; clock.wallTime || (_event.data.wallTime === clock.wallTime &amp;&amp; _event.data.counter &gt; clock.counter)">
        <assign location="clock.wallTime" expr="_event.data.wallTime"/>
        <assign location="clock.counter" expr="_event.data.counter"/>
      </if>
    </transition>

    <!-- The next operation of `taking`, taken in: a write gives its register one more
         value, once, and a write-over takes the value it names out. This is where every
         operation is merged, a copy's own and a peer's alike, a recalled one and a state
         handed over, and it keeps nothing of an operation but its effect, and, for a
         change taken in provisionally, what its write-overs take out.

         A write: its dot is the change's (`dot`), or, in a state handed over
         (`restoring`), the dot it carries. Unless its value is held already, its add is
         added and its value kept, which is told to the parent (record_list.announce). The
         text is read into the value it is kept in. -->
    <transition event="record_list.take" type="internal">
      <assign location="op" expr="taking[took]"/>
      <assign location="took" expr="took + 1"/>
      <assign location="entry.element" expr="op.id"/>
      <assign location="entry.element" expr="entry.element * 65536 + op.field"/>
      <if cond="op.kind === 0">
        <assign location="held.text" expr="op.text"/>
        <assign location="held.id" expr="op.id"/>
        <assign location="held.field" expr="op.field"/>
        <assign location="held.value" expr="op.value"/>
        <assign location="held.wallTime" expr="dot.wallTime"/>
        <assign location="held.counter" expr="dot.counter"/>
        <assign location="held.nodeId" expr="dot.nodeId"/>
        <if cond="restoring">
          <assign location="held.wallTime" expr="op.wallTime"/>
          <assign location="held.counter" expr="op.counter"/>
          <assign location="held.nodeId" expr="op.nodeId"/>
        </if>
        <assign location="entry.wallTime" expr="held.wallTime"/>
        <assign location="entry.counter" expr="held.counter"/>
        <assign location="entry.nodeId" expr="held.nodeId"/>
        <assign location="present" expr="MvValueHolds(values, held)"/>
        <if cond="!present">
          <sce:clear target="one"/>
          <sce:append target="one" expr="entry"/>
          <assign location="adds" expr="OrsetUnion(adds, one)"/>
          <assign location="values" expr="MvValueKeep(values, held)"/>
        </if>
        <if cond="!present &amp;&amp; announce">
          <send target="#_internal" event="record_list.announce">
            <param name="id" expr="op.id"/>
            <param name="field" expr="op.field"/>
          </send>
        </if>
      </if>
      <!-- A write-over: the add of the dot it names leaves `adds` and its value leaves
           `values`, and nothing is kept of it. Its write was given to this copy before it,
           so no later delivery brings the value back. A write-over whose value is gone
           already, because another change wrote it over first, changes nothing and tells
           nothing. A value taken out is told to the parent (record_list.announce).

           A write-over of a change taken in provisionally keeps the value it takes out in
           the undo record, under the change's stamp, so a withdrawal gives it back
           (docs/adr/0093, section 3.4). A write-over whose value is gone already strikes
           the value from the undo record, whatever change it is of: a provisional change
           took the value out first, and another change took it out too, so the value
           stays out whatever is withdrawn. A value is in the undo record only while it is
           out, so the one and the other never meet in one write-over. -->
      <if cond="op.kind === 1">
        <assign location="entry.wallTime" expr="op.wallTime"/>
        <assign location="entry.counter" expr="op.counter"/>
        <assign location="entry.nodeId" expr="op.nodeId"/>
        <assign location="held.id" expr="op.id"/>
        <assign location="held.field" expr="op.field"/>
        <assign location="held.wallTime" expr="op.wallTime"/>
        <assign location="held.counter" expr="op.counter"/>
        <assign location="held.nodeId" expr="op.nodeId"/>
        <assign location="wasLive" expr="MvValueHolds(values, held)"/>
        <if cond="tentative &amp;&amp; wasLive">
          <foreach array="values" item="v">
            <if cond="v.id === held.id &amp;&amp; v.field === held.field &amp;&amp; v.wallTime === held.wallTime &amp;&amp; v.counter === held.counter &amp;&amp; v.nodeId === held.nodeId">
              <assign location="undoing.id" expr="v.id"/>
              <assign location="undoing.field" expr="v.field"/>
              <assign location="undoing.value" expr="v.value"/>
              <assign location="undoing.text" expr="v.text"/>
              <assign location="undoing.wallTime" expr="v.wallTime"/>
              <assign location="undoing.counter" expr="v.counter"/>
              <assign location="undoing.nodeId" expr="v.nodeId"/>
            </if>
          </foreach>
          <assign location="undoing.atWallTime" expr="dot.wallTime"/>
          <assign location="undoing.atCounter" expr="dot.counter"/>
          <sce:append target="undo" expr="undoing"/>
        </if>
        <if cond="!wasLive &amp;&amp; len(undo) &gt; 0">
          <sce:clear target="undoKept"/>
          <foreach array="undo" item="u">
            <if cond="u.id !== held.id || u.field !== held.field || u.wallTime !== held.wallTime || u.counter !== held.counter || u.nodeId !== held.nodeId">
              <sce:append target="undoKept" expr="u"/>
            </if>
          </foreach>
          <sce:clear target="undo"/>
          <foreach array="undoKept" item="u">
            <sce:append target="undo" expr="u"/>
          </foreach>
        </if>
        <sce:clear target="one"/>
        <sce:append target="one" expr="entry"/>
        <assign location="adds" expr="OrsetLive(adds, one)"/>
        <assign location="values" expr="MvValueDrop(values, held)"/>
        <if cond="wasLive &amp;&amp; announce">
          <send target="#_internal" event="record_list.announce">
            <param name="id" expr="op.id"/>
            <param name="field" expr="op.field"/>
          </send>
        </if>
      </if>
    </transition>

    <!-- A change of this copy's own, sent to its peers whole once every operation of it
         is taken in here: its author, its stamp and its operations, in their order. The
         send is the whole of the block, so one that fails where it is made fails alone. -->
    <transition event="record_list.pass" type="internal">
      <send target="#people" event="record_list.change">
        <param name="by" expr="dot.nodeId"/>
        <param name="wallTime" expr="dot.wallTime"/>
        <param name="counter" expr="dot.counter"/>
        <param name="ops" expr="taking"/>
      </send>
    </transition>

    <!-- The host's word that a change the copy took in provisionally is carried now
         (record_confirm, docs/adr/0093, section 3.3): the change leaves `provisional` and
         its values leave the undo record, and the parent is told it is confirmed. A
         confirmation that names no change the copy holds provisionally is the host's
         fault: it changes nothing and is counted. -->
    <transition event="record_list.confirm" type="internal">
      <assign location="provisionalFound" expr="false"/>
      <foreach array="provisional" item="p">
        <if cond="p.wallTime === _event.data.wallTime &amp;&amp; p.counter === _event.data.counter">
          <assign location="provisionalFound" expr="true"/>
          <assign location="standing" expr="p"/>
        </if>
      </foreach>
      <if cond="!provisionalFound">
        <assign location="refusals" expr="refusals + 1"/>
      </if>
      <if cond="provisionalFound">
        <sce:clear target="provisionalKept"/>
        <foreach array="provisional" item="p">
          <if cond="p.wallTime !== standing.wallTime || p.counter !== standing.counter">
            <sce:append target="provisionalKept" expr="p"/>
          </if>
        </foreach>
        <sce:clear target="provisional"/>
        <foreach array="provisionalKept" item="p">
          <sce:append target="provisional" expr="p"/>
        </foreach>
        <sce:clear target="undoKept"/>
        <foreach array="undo" item="u">
          <if cond="u.atWallTime !== standing.wallTime || u.atCounter !== standing.counter">
            <sce:append target="undoKept" expr="u"/>
          </if>
        </foreach>
        <sce:clear target="undo"/>
        <foreach array="undoKept" item="u">
          <sce:append target="undo" expr="u"/>
        </foreach>
        <if cond="announce">
          <send event="record_list.confirmed" targetexpr="'#_parent'" sce:targets="#_parent">
            <param name="wallTime" expr="standing.wallTime"/>
            <param name="counter" expr="standing.counter"/>
            <param name="command" expr="standing.command"/>
          </send>
        </if>
      </if>
    </transition>

    <!-- The host's word that the copy's delivery layer dropped a change the copy took in
         provisionally (record_withdraw, docs/adr/0093, section 3.4): that change and
         every provisional change after it are withdrawn, latest first, each by an event of
         its own (record_list.unwind), since each was prepared on a state that held the
         one before it. A withdrawal that names no change the copy holds provisionally is
         the host's fault: it changes nothing and is counted. -->
    <transition event="record_list.withdraw" type="internal">
      <assign location="provisionalFound" expr="false"/>
      <foreach array="provisional" item="p" index="at">
        <if cond="!provisionalFound &amp;&amp; p.wallTime === _event.data.wallTime &amp;&amp; p.counter === _event.data.counter">
          <assign location="provisionalFound" expr="true"/>
          <assign location="withdrawFrom" expr="at"/>
        </if>
      </foreach>
      <if cond="!provisionalFound">
        <assign location="refusals" expr="refusals + 1"/>
      </if>
      <if cond="provisionalFound">
        <foreach array="provisional" item="p" index="at">
          <if cond="at &gt;= withdrawFrom">
            <send target="#_internal" event="record_list.unwind"/>
          </if>
        </foreach>
      </if>
    </transition>

    <!-- The latest provisional change, withdrawn by its undo record and never by building
         the copy again (docs/adr/0093, section 3.4): every value its writes added (every
         value whose dot is its stamp under this copy's node) goes, every value its
         write-overs took out and no later change took out comes back, and the change and
         its undo record are forgotten. So the copy holds what a copy that never took the
         change in holds, the values in another order. The parent is told each register
         the withdrawals moved once, after the last of them, and `record_list.refused`
         with `peerRefused` and `withdrawn` for the change. The clock is not moved back: a
         stamp is never given twice, even to a change no copy holds. -->
    <transition event="record_list.unwind" type="internal">
      <assign location="standing" expr="provisional[len(provisional) - 1]"/>
      <sce:clear target="one"/>
      <foreach array="adds" item="a">
        <if cond="a.wallTime === standing.wallTime &amp;&amp; a.counter === standing.counter &amp;&amp; a.nodeId === node">
          <sce:append target="one" expr="a"/>
        </if>
      </foreach>
      <assign location="adds" expr="OrsetLive(adds, one)"/>
      <foreach array="one" item="a">
        <assign location="held.id" expr="a.element / 65536"/>
        <assign location="held.field" expr="a.element % 65536"/>
        <assign location="held.wallTime" expr="a.wallTime"/>
        <assign location="held.counter" expr="a.counter"/>
        <assign location="held.nodeId" expr="a.nodeId"/>
        <assign location="values" expr="MvValueDrop(values, held)"/>
        <if cond="announce">
          <assign location="shareId" expr="a.element / 65536"/>
          <assign location="shareField" expr="a.element % 65536"/>
          <send target="#_internal" event="record_list.announce">
            <param name="id" expr="shareId"/>
            <param name="field" expr="shareField"/>
          </send>
        </if>
      </foreach>
      <foreach array="undo" item="u">
        <if cond="u.atWallTime === standing.wallTime &amp;&amp; u.atCounter === standing.counter">
          <assign location="entry.element" expr="u.id"/>
          <assign location="entry.element" expr="entry.element * 65536 + u.field"/>
          <assign location="entry.wallTime" expr="u.wallTime"/>
          <assign location="entry.counter" expr="u.counter"/>
          <assign location="entry.nodeId" expr="u.nodeId"/>
          <sce:clear target="one"/>
          <sce:append target="one" expr="entry"/>
          <assign location="adds" expr="OrsetUnion(adds, one)"/>
          <assign location="held.id" expr="u.id"/>
          <assign location="held.field" expr="u.field"/>
          <assign location="held.value" expr="u.value"/>
          <assign location="held.text" expr="u.text"/>
          <assign location="held.wallTime" expr="u.wallTime"/>
          <assign location="held.counter" expr="u.counter"/>
          <assign location="held.nodeId" expr="u.nodeId"/>
          <assign location="values" expr="MvValueKeep(values, held)"/>
          <if cond="announce">
            <assign location="shareId" expr="u.id"/>
            <assign location="shareField" expr="u.field"/>
            <send target="#_internal" event="record_list.announce">
              <param name="id" expr="shareId"/>
              <param name="field" expr="shareField"/>
            </send>
          </if>
        </if>
      </foreach>
      <sce:clear target="undoKept"/>
      <foreach array="undo" item="u">
        <if cond="u.atWallTime !== standing.wallTime || u.atCounter !== standing.counter">
          <sce:append target="undoKept" expr="u"/>
        </if>
      </foreach>
      <sce:clear target="undo"/>
      <foreach array="undoKept" item="u">
        <sce:append target="undo" expr="u"/>
      </foreach>
      <sce:clear target="provisionalKept"/>
      <foreach array="provisional" item="p" index="at">
        <if cond="at + 1 &lt; len(provisional)">
          <sce:append target="provisionalKept" expr="p"/>
        </if>
      </foreach>
      <sce:clear target="provisional"/>
      <foreach array="provisionalKept" item="p">
        <sce:append target="provisional" expr="p"/>
      </foreach>
      <if cond="announce">
        <send event="record_list.refused" targetexpr="'#_parent'" sce:targets="#_parent">
          <param name="id" expr="standing.id"/>
          <param name="field" expr="standing.field"/>
          <param name="kind" expr="standing.kind"/>
          <param name="reason" expr="Refusal.peerRefused"/>
          <param name="command" expr="standing.command"/>
          <param name="withdrawn" expr="true"/>
        </send>
      </if>
    </transition>

    <!-- A register the change in hand moved, named to be told: kept in `moved` once,
         and for the first one named `record_list.tell` is raised, which waits behind
         every event the change has raised already and so is taken when the change is
         whole. Taken only when a parent started the list asking for it (`announce`): a
         list a host started keeps nothing to tell, whatever raised this. -->
    <transition event="record_list.announce" cond="announce" type="internal">
      <assign location="entry.element" expr="_event.data.id"/>
      <assign location="entry.element" expr="entry.element * 65536 + _event.data.field"/>
      <assign location="listed" expr="false"/>
      <foreach array="moved" item="named">
        <if cond="named === entry.element">
          <assign location="listed" expr="true"/>
        </if>
      </foreach>
      <if cond="len(moved) === 0">
        <send target="#_internal" event="record_list.tell"/>
      </if>
      <if cond="!listed">
        <sce:append target="moved" expr="entry.element"/>
      </if>
    </transition>

    <!-- What each register the change moved holds, told to the statechart that invoked
         the list: the first of its live values in the order of their dots with how many
         there are, then each further one with its place, or a count of 0 and the empty
         value when it holds none. `#_parent` is named among the routes the send declares
         and not written as its target, so the machine keeps the entry a host starts it
         by. -->
    <transition event="record_list.tell" cond="announce" type="internal">
      <foreach array="moved" item="named">
        <assign location="shareId" expr="named / 65536"/>
        <assign location="shareField" expr="named % 65536"/>
        <assign location="live" expr="RegisterValues(values, shareId, shareField)"/>
        <if cond="len(live) === 0">
          <send event="record_list.register" targetexpr="'#_parent'" sce:targets="#_parent">
            <param name="id" expr="shareId"/>
            <param name="field" expr="shareField"/>
            <param name="count" expr="0"/>
            <param name="value" expr="empty.value"/>
            <param name="text" expr="empty.text"/>
            <param name="wallTime" expr="empty.wallTime"/>
            <param name="counter" expr="empty.counter"/>
            <param name="nodeId" expr="empty.nodeId"/>
          </send>
          <assign location="announced" expr="announced + 1"/>
        </if>
        <assign location="ordinal" expr="0"/>
        <foreach array="live" item="r">
          <if cond="ordinal === 0">
            <send event="record_list.register" targetexpr="'#_parent'" sce:targets="#_parent">
              <param name="id" expr="shareId"/>
              <param name="field" expr="shareField"/>
              <param name="count" expr="len(live)"/>
              <param name="value" expr="r.value"/>
              <param name="text" expr="r.text"/>
              <param name="wallTime" expr="r.wallTime"/>
              <param name="counter" expr="r.counter"/>
              <param name="nodeId" expr="r.nodeId"/>
            </send>
          </if>
          <if cond="ordinal !== 0">
            <send event="record_list.value" targetexpr="'#_parent'" sce:targets="#_parent">
              <param name="id" expr="shareId"/>
              <param name="field" expr="shareField"/>
              <param name="ordinal" expr="ordinal"/>
              <param name="value" expr="r.value"/>
              <param name="text" expr="r.text"/>
              <param name="wallTime" expr="r.wallTime"/>
              <param name="counter" expr="r.counter"/>
              <param name="nodeId" expr="r.nodeId"/>
            </send>
          </if>
          <assign location="announced" expr="announced + 1"/>
          <assign location="ordinal" expr="ordinal + 1"/>
        </foreach>
      </foreach>
      <sce:clear target="moved"/>
    </transition>

    <!-- Every failure is counted. One a command or the end of a change met while it was
         staging the change or turning it into its operations (`probing`) refuses the
         change: a change past the room of `staged` or of `taking`. A command whose
         delivery is outside its type is refused where it is read, never reaches the
         change, and is counted here all the same. The block it stood in has ended, so a
         command that ended the change has its end raised here, where the change is
         refused whole. -->
    <transition event="error.execution" type="internal">
      <assign location="refusals" expr="refusals + 1"/>
      <if cond="probing">
        <assign location="probing" expr="false"/>
        <assign location="spoiled" expr="true"/>
        <assign location="spoiledFor" expr="probe"/>
        <if cond="!holding">
          <send target="#_internal" event="record_list.close"/>
        </if>
      </if>
    </transition>
  </state>
</scxml>
